         "statement": "Let $Y$ be a closed connected oriented rational homology three-sphere, let $\\mathfrak t$ be a Spin$^c$ structure, and suppose the Heegaard Floer groups, absolute rational grading, and natural map $\\iota_*:HF^\\infty(Y,\\mathfrak t)\\to HF^+(Y,\\mathfrak t)$ are defined and independent of the construction choices. View $HF^+$ as an $\\mathbb F_2[U]$-module. An element is $U$-torsion if some positive power of $U$ annihilates it. The correction term $d(Y,\\mathfrak t)$ is the minimum absolute grading of a nonzero homogeneous element in $\\operatorname{im}\\iota_*$. In the standard plus tower every element is $U$-torsion, although every element is divisible by every positive power of $U$; these two properties are compatible. The definition uses the nonzero homogeneous image elements, rather than imposing $U$-nontorsion. The standard normalization is $d(S^3,\\mathfrak t_0)=0$ for the unique Spin$^c$ structure $\\mathfrak t_0$ on $S^3$. Existence of the minimum and independence of choices are separate proof obligations.",
